WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:06.029
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie, this week for
Game of Thrones bonus time I wanted to talk

00:00:06.029 --> 00:00:07.990
about some of my favorite character pairings.

00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:12.740
The show and the books are already very different
but it gives us more opportunities to spend

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:14.410
time with people.

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:21.480
It’s one of the only benefits of narrowing
down plotlines and cutting out secondary characters.

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:24.360
It just gives you more time with the people
they keep.

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:25.890
So these are my top 5 pairings from the show.

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:29.460
But I’ll try to squeeze some book in here
for extra context.

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:33.500
Oh and new round of the book giveaway today,
all you have to do to enter is be a subscriber

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:35.050
and leave a comment on this video.

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:39.170
Careful For Spoilers for everything through
season 4 on the show.

00:00:39.170 --> 00:00:40.670
I’ll wait just a sec...okay.

00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:41.670
Here we go.

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:43.970
Number 5 - Jaime and Cersei

00:00:43.970 --> 00:00:47.810
I always love watching interviews where people
asks Lena Headey and Nikolaj Coster Waldeau

00:00:47.810 --> 00:00:57.230
about 
Jaime Cersei motivations.

00:00:57.230 --> 00:01:10.290
They’re definitely one of the most interesting
couples, and no matter what, I don’t think

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:14.470
either one of them will be able to unwind
their relationship.

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:16.620
At least completely.

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:21.210
They’re twins, so even if they didn’t
have a sexual relationship, they’d still

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:27.420
have that pseudo psychic shared twin space
in their heads.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:33.040
I know everyone was really upset with what
the show did with them this year, especially

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:34.210
Jaime.

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:39.850
It did seem like he was on something of a
redemptive arc, cut to twincest over their

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:41.040
dead son’s body.

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:44.659
I don’t think it would have been very interesting
if Jaime had automatically turned into a boy

00:01:44.659 --> 00:01:46.830
scout during the back half of season 3.

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:49.770
Not that the possibility is completely gone.

00:01:49.770 --> 00:02:00.680
I just think that everyone in that family
is doomed to wallow in their misery.

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:05.340
Regardless of what happens to either character,
the Jaime/Cersei pairing is part of the bedrock

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:07.040
of the series.

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:10.270
The books go in a slightly different direction
after that big sex scene over Joffrey’s

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:15.480
body, so I’ll be interested to see if George
RR Martin backtracks in Winds of Winter or

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:16.480
future books.

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:20.590
Right now neither one of them is a confirmed
POV character in the next book, so we might

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:23.280
not get to spend as much time with them.

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:25.650
Number 4 - Jon and Ygritte

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:28.860
They spent a lot more time together in the
books so I was a little dissapointed that

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:38.030
Ygritte’s teachings didn’t become as big
a thing on the show.

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:50.770
They made Jon’s sexual education a big thing
but their relationship went way beyond that.

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:55.920
Jon had this really rapid period of mind expansion
while he was north of the wall.

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:59.360
If you’re looking at it from a Hero’s
Journey Joseph Campbell perspective, Ygritte

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:00.740
was his Goddess.

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:02.410
She imparted great wisdom.

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:04.960
Sexual wisdom yes, but also cultural wisdom.

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:09.330
It’s like being a foreign exchange student
and coming to the realization that you only

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:11.960
learned a fraction of the real truth of the
world.

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:18.569
In a funny way, you could look at the climbing
of the wall as this crazy drug trip they did

00:03:18.569 --> 00:03:19.569
together.

00:03:19.569 --> 00:03:24.030
Like they both dropped ecstacy and the process
of climbing the wall was the drugs opening

00:03:24.030 --> 00:03:25.030
Jon’s mind.

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:29.489
And just as they hit the top and you get that
big wide shot south of the wall, Jon comes

00:03:29.489 --> 00:03:34.349
to this big realization.

00:03:34.349 --> 00:03:38.520
I think the sex in the cave was the same thing
for him, as was Ygritte’s death.

00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:42.879
Now that she’s gone or at least physically
gone.

00:03:42.879 --> 00:03:46.260
I’ll be interested to see the Jon/Melisandre
pairing.

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:51.060
I feel like that long look over the fire was
a big teaser for some amazing scenes in season

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:52.060
5.

00:03:52.060 --> 00:03:55.680
I don’t think the show will take it to a
Gendry Melisandre Sexual place, but still.

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:58.470
Something is going to happen with those two.

00:03:58.470 --> 00:04:00.370
Number 3 - Stannis and Melisandre

00:04:00.370 --> 00:04:04.550
I always feel like Melisandre is playing games
with everyone, so even though she and Stannis

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:12.599
have a very toxic Jaime Cersei type relationship,
Stannis is always going to be the subordinate.

00:04:12.599 --> 00:04:14.940
Let’s be honest about who the brains of
that operation is.

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:17.239
I think he’s completely at her mercy.

00:04:17.239 --> 00:04:25.379
Jaime Cersei is a little more balanced, Stannis
always seemed to me like he was written so

00:04:25.379 --> 00:04:32.509
that you wouldn’t route for him.

00:04:32.509 --> 00:04:37.600
Sometimes I get the sense that in the narrative,
the character feels that way about himself.

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:44.020
Like history is being written, he’s a secondary
character and that pisses him off so he takes

00:04:44.020 --> 00:04:45.229
up with Melisandre.

00:04:45.229 --> 00:04:48.490
But he reekes of desperation and neediness.

00:04:48.490 --> 00:04:53.199
Which are two of the most unattractive qualities,
so anytime he’s on screen with someone else,

00:04:53.199 --> 00:04:55.279
you automatically root for the other person.

00:04:55.279 --> 00:04:58.389
So naturally it seems like we’re always
supposed to root for Melisandre.

00:04:58.389 --> 00:05:00.969
Number 2 - Jaime and Brienne

00:05:00.969 --> 00:05:03.819
Probably one of my favorite tragic couples
on tv right now.

00:05:03.819 --> 00:05:07.879
Just two people that seem like they bring
out so much potential in each other, but because

00:05:07.879 --> 00:05:11.509
it’s Martin writing the story, you get the
sense that they’ll never get the happily

00:05:11.509 --> 00:05:12.509
ever after ending.

00:05:12.509 --> 00:05:15.520
There is no Disney ending for anyone in a
song of ice and fire.

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:22.409
That’s not a bad thing, I think knowing
they’ll probably never consummate their

00:05:22.409 --> 00:05:24.899
relationship makes their scenes more electric.

00:05:24.899 --> 00:05:43.129
I’m actually really happy with the way the
show changed Brienne’s character.

00:05:43.129 --> 00:05:49.600
The’re a giant plotline that was excised
when they didn’t do Lady Stoneheart in season

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:53.129
4, so I’m curious to see if they continue
to go in a different direction with Jaime

00:05:53.129 --> 00:05:58.240
and Brienne or if they circle back around
to the book story in a creative way.

00:05:58.240 --> 00:06:02.669
Sometimes when they change things on the show,
like the whole Bran Karl Tanner storyline,

00:06:02.669 --> 00:06:05.180
they still get to the same destination.

00:06:05.180 --> 00:06:07.360
Bran still ended up meeting the Bloodraven.

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:11.979
I’m really hoping we get to see some crossover
between the Brienne storyline and the Sansa

00:06:11.979 --> 00:06:12.979
Littlefinger storyline.

00:06:12.979 --> 00:06:14.240
And I do know they’re making a few big changes
to Jaime’s story in book 4.

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:19.460
I do not think Brienne will head back to King’s
Landing even though Arya Stark slipped through

00:06:19.460 --> 00:06:21.159
her fingers.

00:06:21.159 --> 00:06:28.149
Speaking of which, my Number 1 pairing - Arya
and The Hound, Team Fuck the King

00:06:28.149 --> 00:06:33.589
For all the changes they made in the story,
their arc in season 4 felt pretty close to

00:06:33.589 --> 00:06:34.589
the books.

00:06:34.589 --> 00:06:38.960
There were a lot of minor details that were
off, like the timing and cause of their split,

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:40.919
but Arya still came to the same conclusion.

00:06:40.919 --> 00:06:43.319
She just stopped giving a shit about him.

00:06:43.319 --> 00:06:48.279
I think part of the reason they were my favorite
pair is because they seemed like such an odd

00:06:48.279 --> 00:06:51.279
couple, but they brought out the best in each
other.

00:06:51.279 --> 00:06:55.249
Arya learned where the heart is, just a good
metaphor for growing up.

00:06:55.249 --> 00:07:02.789
And The Hound found something that made him
feel like less of a dirtbag.

00:07:02.789 --> 00:07:09.199
The Hound never quite crossed that bridge
so to speak, which is why Arya had to leave

00:07:09.199 --> 00:07:10.199
him.

00:07:10.199 --> 00:07:13.869
I know there are a lot of Gravedigger theories
that he might still be alive and get a measure

00:07:13.869 --> 00:07:16.450
of redemption, but at least he helped Arya
evolve.

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:24.119
Two of my favorite moments just from season
4 in general were when Arya killed Polliver

00:07:24.119 --> 00:07:29.800
and Rorge and I don’t think she would have
become that person without The Hound’s influence.

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:37.169
It’s also important to note that when Arya
left the Hound, she was just leaving him to

00:07:37.169 --> 00:07:38.969
his fate live or die.

00:07:38.969 --> 00:07:41.919
I don’t think she thought, “He’s Dead”.

00:07:41.919 --> 00:07:44.960
She was just done with him.

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:46.759
But she did not cross him off her list.

00:07:46.759 --> 00:07:49.659
He’s still on her list, so I think someday,
if he does come back.

00:07:49.659 --> 00:07:51.129
She’ll still kill him.

00:07:51.129 --> 00:07:55.509
It’s totally possible that even if the Hound
does survive, he could be completely omitted

00:07:55.509 --> 00:07:58.729
from Season 5, like they’ll just not use
his character.

00:07:58.729 --> 00:08:01.520
They’re doing the same thing with Hodor.

